# The app's environment for the smoke step and the contact sheet
# (tools/verify/smoke, tools/verify/contact-sheet): one NAME=value per line, set
# for their next build and next start, so the gate's answer doesn't hang on what
# a live service holds today. Blank lines and # comments are ignored; NAME is
# capitals, digits and _, not starting with a digit, and none of the steps' own
# (NX_*, FACTORY_*). The value is the rest of the line, as written. In it the
# step puts:
#   {fixtures}  the Scenario driver's fixture server (_scenario_fixtures.mjs),
#               http://127.0.0.1:<port>, on a port the OS picks free, the same
#               for the build and the start; it starts only when a value names
#               it. It serves the committed files of tools/verify/smoke-fixtures/:
#               the file smoke-fixtures/<path> at {fixtures}/<path> (any depth;
#               its Content-Type by its extension: .ics text/calendar, .json
#               application/json, .html text/html, .xml application/xml, .txt
#               text/plain, else application/octet-stream), and nothing else.
#               Each {fixtures}/<path> a value names must be a file there, with
#               no query after it (the server would answer 404; a #fragment
#               isn't sent, so it may follow), or it's a finding.
#   {state}     a folder of the step's own, empty at its start, gone at its end
# For example, an app that reads a feed and keeps a cache:
#   FEED_URL={fixtures}/feed.ics       (and tools/verify/smoke-fixtures/feed.ics)
#   CACHE_PATH={state}/cache.sqlite
# Date what a fixture holds so the pages it gives never change: events far in
# the future (2099), and past ones only as the app needs them.
# None by default: the app runs as its own config says, and no fixture server
# starts.

# The calendar feed from the fixture server (tools/verify/smoke-fixtures/
# calendar.ics: one event long past and four in 2099, so the Upcoming strip
# shows the same four cards whatever the date), and a cache of the step's own
# (src/server/calendar/).
CALENDAR_FEED_URL={fixtures}/calendar.ics
EVENTS_CACHE_PATH={state}/events.sqlite
